R"VG(
# prehistoric8.vg (H-04's second pass): the years' events as the prehistoric songs sang them (`@event ... pre.song`), three lines
# and the people's refrain: the flood, the hunger, the sickness, the fight between bands, the coming into the land, the stones, the
# herds that came late or did not come, the storm, the fire, the gathering. Every line carries something of the people's own.

@root pre.song.*

pre.song.flood
  {pre.sf.a}\n{pre.sf.b}\n{pre.sf.c}\n{pre.refrain}
pre.sf.a
  The water came up at {$e.place}, the water came up over the {crop},
  {river} left its bed in {$e.season} and came for us,
  It rained on {land} and it rained, and {river} was hungry,
  We heard it in the night, the water talking under {house.one.lc},
pre.sf.b
  it took {houses} and it took the {herd},
  we carried the fire up the hill in {vessel.one},
  the children on our backs and the old ones on the {herd},
  it took the drying racks and the winter's {food},
pre.sf.c
  and when it went down it went down in a new place, and the {tree} with it,
  and we came back and built {houses} again in the mud,
  and the old ones said it had happened when {river} was smaller,
  and we counted the {herd} on the hill, and the people, and someone was not,

pre.song.famine
  There was no {crop} in {$e.season}, there was no {crop},\n{pre.sfam.b}\n{pre.sfam.c}\n{pre.refrain}
  {pre.sfam.a}\n{pre.sfam.b}\n{pre.sfam.c}\n{pre.refrain}
pre.sfam.a
  The {game} went away from {land} and did not come back,
  The {vessel} were empty by the middle of {season.now},
  The {herd} were thin and then the {herd} were gone,
pre.sfam.b
  we ate the seed and then we ate the {tree.n} bark,
  we boiled the hides and drank the water from {watersrc},
  the dogs went first, and then the old ones,
  the children cried for {food} and then the children were quiet,
pre.sfam.c
  {#$e.value:about} went hungry to {deadplace},
  and we sing it so nobody forgets to fill the {vessel},
  and the ones who lived are the ones who sing to {god},

pre.song.sickness
  {pre.ssk.a}\n{pre.ssk.b}\n{pre.ssk.c}\n{pre.refrain}
pre.ssk.a
  {$e.sickness} came to {$e.place}, nobody asked it in,
  ($e.wave>1) {$e.sickness} came back, as it always comes back,
  {$e.sickness} came in {$e.season} with the traders and their {trade.thing},
  It came at night, it sat by every {fuel} fire,
pre.ssk.b
  it took the old ones first, and then the ones who fed the {herd},
  the hot ones lay in {houses} and the cold ones lay outside,
  we burned the {fuel} with the bitter smoke and it did not care,
  nobody went to {watersrc}, nobody went to the {herd},
pre.ssk.c
  {#$e.value:about} we carried out to {deadplace},
  and the camp at {$e.place} was moved, and {houses} left standing empty,
  and the ones who lived wear {colour.mourn} for it still,

pre.song.battle
  {pre.sb.a}\n{pre.sb.b}\n{pre.sb.c}\n{pre.refrain}
pre.sb.a
  At {$e.place} in {$e.season} the bands stood with {pre.weapon},
  They came over {land} to {$e.place} with their faces painted,
  Who was at {$e.place}? Ask the ones who came home,
  We went down to {$e.place} with {pre.weapon} and shouting,
pre.sb.b
  ($e.won=1) and they broke and ran back over the hill;
  ($e.won=1) and by dark {watersrc} was ours again;
  ($e.won=0) and they were too many, and we came home few;
  ($e.won=0) and they took the {herd} and the good ground;
  ($e.won=draw) and neither gave, and both went home at dark;
pre.sb.c
  {#$e.value:about} lay down there and did not get up,
  the {bird} came down on {$e.place} for days,
  and the women went out to look for faces, in {colour.mourn},
  and nobody remembers now if it was for the water or the {herd},

pre.song.war
  {pre.sw.a}\n{pre.sw.b}\n{pre.sw.c}\n{pre.refrain}
pre.sw.a
  The quarrel began over {$e.place} and {watersrc} there,
  ($e.warkind=other|$e.warkind=conquest) The {other} came out of the hills with their {pre.weapon},
  It began with a {beast} taken and a word said,
pre.sw.b
  and the young ones painted their arms {colour.holy} and went,
  and the old ones said it would not last the season,
  and the fires on the hills of {land} were lit every night,
pre.sw.c
  and nobody remembers who threw the first {pre.weapon.one},
  and it lasted longer than the old ones said,
  and the children played at it with sticks after, which was worse,

pre.song.sack
  They came to {$e.place} at night with fire,\n{houses} burned and the {herd} were driven off,\n{pre.ssack.c}\n{pre.refrain}
pre.ssack.c
  and who was inside, ask the ashes,
  and the ones who ran over {land} are the ones who sing,
  and we did not go back to {$e.place} after,

pre.song.coming
  {pre.scm.a}\n{pre.scm.b}\n{pre.scm.c}\n{pre.refrain}
pre.scm.a
  We came into the land {pre.whence},
  Long ago, before the stones, we came {pre.whence},
  The first ones walked {pre.whence} with nothing,
pre.whence
  ($e.whence=mountain) over {mountain}
  ($e.whence=sea) over {sea}
  ($e.whence=north) out of the north
  ($e.whence=south) out of the south
  ($e.whence=east|$e.whence=west) from where the sun goes
  ($e.whence=river) down {river}
  ($e.whence=dry) across the dry country
  (!has:$e.whence) from far away
pre.scm.b
  we came with the {herd} and the fire in {vessel.one},
  the old ones carried the bones of the older ones in {vessel},
  we had {tool} and the dogs and our names,
pre.scm.c
  and the land was empty and the land was good, full of {game},
  and the first one said, here, and it was here,
  and the {game} did not know us yet,

pre.song.stones
  We raised the stones where {city} would be,\n{#number} stones for the {#number} winds,\n{pre.sst.c}\n{pre.refrain}
  We dragged the stones on rollers from the hill,\nwe sang to pull and pulled to sing, with {instrument},\n{pre.sst.c}\n{pre.refrain}
pre.sst.c
  and they stand there still, and we are still here,
  and the shadows tell us when {festival} comes,
  and the dead sit inside the ring at night, in {colour.mourn},

pre.song.founding
  {$e.a:name} came to {$e.place} when there was nothing there,\nonly the {tree} and the water and the wind,\nand said: here, and it was here,\n{pre.refrain}
  {pre.sfo.a}\n{pre.sfo.b}\n{pre.refrain}
pre.sfo.a
  They put up the first {pre.hut.n} at {$e.place} in {$e.season},
  The first fire at {$e.place} was lit from the old fire in {vessel.one},
pre.sfo.b
  and the {herd} were put in a ring of thorns, and the children ran,
  and {$e.place} has been there since, as long as anyone counts the {herd},

pre.song.winter
  The winter came and the winter stayed,\n{pre.swi.b}\n{pre.swi.c}\n{pre.refrain}
pre.swi.b
  the {crop} lay under the snow until it rotted,
  the {game} went south and did not come back,
  the ice came into {houses} at night,
pre.swi.c
  and we burned everything that would burn, and then the {tree},
  and {skyone} was small and pale all year,
  and the old ones gave their {food} to the young,

pre.song.drought
  No rain, no rain, {watersrc} gave sand,\nthe {herd} lay down in the dry beds of the streams,\n{pre.sdr.c}\n{pre.refrain}
  The sky was white for {#$e.value|year} and the ground was cracked,\nwe dug for water with {tool} and found dust,\n{pre.sdr.c}\n{pre.refrain}
pre.sdr.c
  and we went to the far water with the {herd}, and some did not get there,
  and when the rain came we stood in it with our mouths open,

pre.song.quake
  The ground at {$e.place} turned over in its sleep,\nand {houses} came down on the ones inside,\nand we dug with our hands until {skyone} rose,\n{pre.refrain}
  The ground shook at {$e.place} like a dog shaking water,\nthe {herd} ran and {houses} fell flat,\nand {river} ran the wrong way for a day,\n{pre.refrain}
pre.song.eruption
  {mountain} woke up angry, {mountain} woke up red,\nand the ash came down on {$e.place} like snow that does not melt,\n{pre.refrain}
  Fire came out of the top of the hill at {$e.place},\nthe night was day and the day was night,\nand we ran, and the {herd} ran faster,\n{pre.refrain}
pre.song.impact
  A stone came down from the sky at {$e.place},\nand the sky went dark and the {crop} did not come,\n{pre.refrain}

pre.song.rulerdeath
  {pre.srd.a}\n{pre.srd.b}\n{pre.srd.c}\n{pre.refrain}
pre.srd.a
  {$e.a:full} is dead, and the fires are put out for {$e.a:obj},
  They carried {$e.a:full} out at first light on {pre.bier},
  Who will sit where {$e.a:name} sat, at the head of the fire,
  {$e.a:name} has {death.went}, and the {herd} are crying,
pre.srd.b
  {$e.a:name} who led us {#$e.a.reigned:words|year},
  {$e.a:name} who knew every path to {mountain},
  {$e.a:name} who was hard, and was fair, mostly, over the {herd},
  and {$e.a:poss} {pre.weapon.one} is laid down beside {$e.a:obj},
pre.srd.c
  and nobody speaks at the fire tonight,
  and the young ones look at each other and wait,
  and the women keen at the door in {colour.mourn} till dawn,
  and the new one is afraid, and should be,
pre.song.death
  {$e.a:full} is gone, who was known to all,\nthey carried {$e.a:obj} up to {deadplace} with {instrument},\n{pre.refrain}

pre.song.omen
  ($e.omen=comet) The hairy star came back as the old ones said,\nand we stood in the {crop} and watched it pass,\n{pre.refrain}
  ($e.omen=eclipse) The sun went out in the middle of the day,\nand the {bird} went to sleep and the dogs howled,\nand then it came back, and we sang this,\n{pre.refrain}
  ($e.omen!=comet $e.omen!=eclipse) There was a sign in the sky over {$e.place},\nand the old ones said this and the old ones said that over the {food},\n{pre.refrain}
  ($e.omen=wanderer 3) The wanderer grew bigger over {$e.place} every night,\nand the old ones said it was coming for the {herd},\n{pre.refrain}
  ($e.omen=intruder 3) A new sun came up where no sun was,\nand the old ones put out their fires and watched it,\n{pre.refrain}
  ($e.omen=dance 3) The second sun went further off each summer,\nand the children asked where it was going,\n{pre.refrain}
  ($e.omen=bent 3) The stars moved out of their places over {$e.place},\nand nobody could find the way by them,\n{pre.refrain}
pre.song.contact
  Over the hills there were others, and we did not know,\nthey were taller than us and their {pre.weapon} were longer,\nand they held out their hands, and we held out {trade.thing},\n{pre.refrain}
pre.song.exodus
  They left {$e.place} with the {herd} and the fire,\nand they did not look back, and we did not wave,\n{pre.refrain}

# the everyday, sung
pre.song.beasts
  ($e.what=late) We waited on the ridge and the {game} did not come,\nwe waited till {season.next} and then they came,\nlate, late, and thin, and we were glad,\n{pre.refrain}
  ($e.what=early) The {game} came early, before the {pre.weapon} were ready,\nwe ran out with the children's spears and the old ones' spears,\n{pre.refrain}
  ($e.what=none) The {game} did not come, the {game} did not come,\nwe sang to them with {instrument} and they did not come,\nwe ate the {herd} and the {crop} and the dogs looked at us,\n{pre.refrain}
  ($e.what=many) The {game} came down over {land} like a river,\nso many the ground shook, so many we stopped counting,\n{pre.refrain}
  ($e.what=great) The great {game.one} came to {$e.place},\nas high as {pre.hut.n}, and its breath was smoke,\nand we took it, and the camp ate for a moon,\n{pre.refrain}
  ($e.what=killed) The {game.one} turned at {$e.place}, the {game.one} turned,\nand the hunter in front did not get out of the way,\n{pre.refrain}
pre.song.storm
  ($e.what=wind) The wind came and took the {roofs} off {$e.place},\nand we held the hides down with our bodies all night,\n{pre.refrain}
  ($e.what=hail) Stones of ice came down on {$e.place} in {$e.season},\nand the {crop2} lay flat and the {herd} ran,\n{pre.refrain}
  ($e.what=snow) The snow came up to the {roofs} at {$e.place},\nand we dug out the {herd} one by one, and some were sleeping,\n{pre.refrain}
  ($e.what=dust) The dust came out of {land} and the day went brown,\nand we tied {material} over our mouths and waited,\n{pre.refrain}
  ($e.what=sea|$e.what=rain|$e.what=lightning) The sky broke open over {$e.place},\nand the water and the fire came down together on the {tree},\n{pre.refrain}
pre.song.fire
  The grass burned from {mountain} to the water,\nwe stood in {river} and watched it go by,\n{pre.refrain}
  The fire got into {houses} at {$e.place} at night,\nwe carried out the children and the {vessel}, and then nothing,\n{pre.refrain}
pre.song.wonder
  At {$e.place} there was a thing nobody had seen,\nand the old ones said it meant this and that over the {food},\nand nothing came of it, and we sing it anyway,\n{pre.refrain}
pre.song.games
  (has:$e.a) They ran at {$e.place} from the stone to the {tree.n},\nand {$e.a:name} was in front, and the dogs ran too,\n{pre.refrain}
  They ran at {$e.place} from the stone to the {tree.n},\nand the old ones bet {vessel} on it,\n{pre.refrain}
  (has:$e.a) They wrestled at {$e.place} by the {fuel} fire,\nand {$e.a:name} threw them all, one after another,\n{pre.refrain}
pre.song.fair
  All the bands came to {$e.place} with their things,\nwe traded {trade.thing} and we traded songs,\nand three girls of {$home} went home with other bands,\n{pre.refrain}
pre.song.pest
  The {pest} came in {$e.season} and ate the {crop2},\nwe beat the ground and shouted, and they ate the {crop2},\n{pre.refrain}
pre.song.none
  {pre.sh.land}
)VG"
